    <informations>Shelly EM Gen3 — mounting plate, back view.
Terminals, left to right as printed: O I IB.1 IB.2 IA.1 IA.2 L N.
Back view: the terminal order is mirrored against the front label face.

Official sources:
https://kb.shelly.cloud/knowledge-base/shelly-em-gen3
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_757e383b761814702b048f71d05cbe3a90e60021ccf0853196accf015ba2aa02/Shelly%20EM%20Gen3_front%20view.jpg?cb=195722c61f949a70dbd382d190eb1520
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_d3da7d196db1e6e76f038fc886be8b42e05fe289d729584201996d4f31fc24df/EM-Gen3-internal-schematics.png?cb=de92b7bb1496610f41d15439b4e1d8f3
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_606aced287946c1d6b0408d266558fe9b557e276a23562d70b11eae4d68c69d0/Shelly%20EM%20Gen3%20multilingual%20printed%20user%20and%20safety%20guide.pdf

Notes:
- O/I are the dry-contact relay; IB and IA are two physically distinct two-pin CT sockets, not screw terminals. The left-to-right order is IB before IA.
- CT socket contact names IB.1/IB.2 and IA.1/IA.2 are synthetic unique identifiers for library connectivity, not printed manufacturer polarity labels. No +/− polarity is inferred.

Nominal dimensions and an illustrative outline: corner radii, screw pitch and recesses are drawn to be recognisable, not to manufacturing CAD.</informations>
